# runtime/jit_toolchain: the rewriter, E9Tool plugin and runtime that build the whole-program Fast images of the JIT
# suites (Java/Renaissance, Node).
# They add, over runtime/rewrite.py + runtime/rt + runtime/e9plugin (which build the non-JIT Fast images): per-thread
# keyframe counters in the %gs block (rewrite.py --kf-gs/--kf-base; runtime PTLOG_KF_N), --reserve-cursor, buffer
# recycling (PTLOG_RECYCLE), thread-exit headroom (ptlogmt.c -> ptlogrt.c), and the JIT arm entry point the V8 hook /
# JVMTI agent resolve (ptlog_jit_arm).
# Used by run/lib/jitwp/build_images.sh (rewrite.py) and run/lib/repslice.py e9fast (LD_PRELOAD rt/ptlogmt.so:rt/ptlogrt.so).
# Built by ptracer/build.sh (make -C runtime/jit_toolchain/e9plugin) with the artifact's E9Patch; rewrite.py does not
# use E9Patch's CFR/relocation-map options, so they are inactive for these images.
# rewrite.py and e9plugin/ptlog.cpp also support `--sync-carrier tnt' (sync markers in TNT bits, no PTWRITE; default off).
